[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2041888020","html_url":"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1064#issuecomment-2041888020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1064","id":2041888020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOACh1KM55tL0U","user":{"login":"dr-jts","id":3529053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjkwNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts","html_url":"https://github.com/dr-jts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-08T05:23:36Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T18:07:01Z","body":"This is not a bug, but a limitation in the ability to compute the relate matrix due to numeric rounding.  In order to correctly compute the relate matrix for two lines the **node point** must be computed (see https://github.com/locationtech/jts/issues/396 for an example of a case which requires noding for correct evaluation). However, due to numeric roundoff the computed node point equals an **endpoint** of line B, even though the robust `Orientation` test reports that it lies in the **interior** of B.\r\n\r\nIt's not clear that there is an algorithm which can avoid noding, since this would cause an inconsistency in other cases.\r\n\r\nAnother future option is to support evaluating predicates with a distance tolerance.  This will essentially allow avoiding inconsistency due to roundoff.  (However, note that this may not be a solution in itself - when used as part of a bigger process, the entire process must be designed to support using a tolerance.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2041888020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2097681076","html_url":"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1064#issuecomment-2097681076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1064","id":2097681076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOACh1KM59CBK0","user":{"login":"strk","id":289678,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTY3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk","html_url":"https://github.com/strk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-07T07:57:10Z","updated_at":"2024-05-07T07:57:10Z","body":"For the record, GEOS-3.8 gives a different intersection matrix for the two lines, saying there is no interior/boundary intersection. Did 3.8 not have this limitation ?\r\n\r\n```\r\n   I B E\r\nI: F F 1\r\nB: F F 0\r\nE: 1 0 2\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2097681076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2097689307","html_url":"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1064#issuecomment-2097689307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1064","id":2097689307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOACh1KM59CDLb","user":{"login":"strk","id":289678,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTY3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk","html_url":"https://github.com/strk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/strk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-07T08:01:49Z","updated_at":"2024-05-07T08:01:49Z","body":"An XML test for this case was added in #1092 - the test passes in 3.8 branch, fails in main branch:\r\n```\r\nbuild/bin/test_xmltester -v ../3.8/tests/xmltester/tests/issue/issue-geos-gh1064.xml \r\n../3.8/tests/xmltester/tests/issue/issue-geos-gh1064.xml: case1: test1: relatestring(A, B): failed. (0 ms)\r\n        Description: See https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1064\r\n        Geometry A: LINESTRING (16.330791631988802 68.75635661578073, 16.332533