3.8 branch: https://github.com/libgeos/geos/actions/runs/8982102259/job/24668979871?pr=1092#step:4:6239 (PR GH-1092)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2097765768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2098485147","html_url":"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/issues/1064#issuecomment-2098485147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/1064","id":2098485147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOACh1KM59FFeb","user":{"login":"dr-jts","id":3529053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjkwNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3529053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts","html_url":"https://github.com/dr-jts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dr-jts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-07T14:02:15Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T18:06:02Z","body":"> For the record, GEOS-3.8 gives a different intersection matrix for the two lines, saying there is no interior/boundary intersection. Did 3.8 not have this limitation ?\r\n\r\nThis might be due to the change in line intersection computation math, from `ttmath` to `DD` (in https://github.com/libgeos/geos/commit/ec219c058280dae38f338437925c8062fb6b85d7). However, the reason that `DD` was added is that it fixes other cases which were failing using `ttmath`.\r\n\r\nNote that 3.8 is reporting that there is no intersection between the lines at all.  However, the 3.12 `Orientation` predicate is reporting that there is a proper intersection between them (see image below).  This uses the best known algorithm we have, so the only thing we can do is to accept it as the correct analysis of the situation.   So in this case 3.8 is \"wrong\", according to current technology.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"509\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/libgeos/geos/assets/3529053/92802394-9dce-45f4-81cc-925e753d265a\">\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libgeos/geos/issues/comments/2098485147/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]